      "dom_id": "step-q37770",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{3}=4 \\\\ {x}_{2}-5{x}_{3}=3 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{3}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form.",
      "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 & 4 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=-\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
