    "q-131507": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131507",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 8 & -7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 9 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      "worked_solution": "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}7x+8y-7z=5 \\\\ 0x-5y+9z=-8 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=1,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-131507-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "No solution",
              "html": "No solution"
            },
            {
              "option": "b",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-131507-b",
