    "q-10293": {
      "dom_id": "step-q10293",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -6 & 12 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 12 & -16 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -12 & 21\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form, and then find the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      "worked_solution": "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -6 & 12 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 12 & -16 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -12 & 21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 24 & -40 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -12 & 21\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}-{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 8 & 24 & -40 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{8}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -6 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -6 & 12 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y-6z=12 \\\\ 0x+y+3z=-5 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=-1,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-10293-a",
