    "q-131519": {
      "dom_id": "step-q131519",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 6 & -7 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix.",
      "worked_solution": "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+6y-7z=4 \\\\ 0x+3y+0z=9 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=-8,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
